d medal away, as he won by almost 1½ seconds. Kühl passed Yaroshchuk on the final lap for silver."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Darnyi had won the 200/400 IM double. Four years later, in Seoul, he would win the two events again, becoming only the second man, after East German " [:a {:href "/athletes/47595"} "Roland Matthes"] " in the 1968/72 backstroke events, to double-double in a stroke or specialty. This would later be repeated in the IMs by Ukrainian " [:a {:href "/athletes/93833"} "Yana Klochkova"] " in 2000-04."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "B Final"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "305"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/48168"} "Tamás Darnyi"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/HUN.png"}] "HUN"]] [:td {} "2:02.15 (1 h8)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "2:00.17 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "261"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/47860"} "Patrick Kühl"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GDR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GDR.png"}] "GDR"]] [:td {} "2:03.77 (1 h6)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "2:01.61 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "518"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/50815"} "Vadim Yaroshchuk"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} "2:02.77 (2 h8)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "2:02.40 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [: